  "title": "Whole-profile lower layer: deformation and matching screen",
  "description": "Nine 1024\u00b2 runs compare deformation radii of 2,000, 3,200 and 4,000 km with prescribed lower flows equal to 0, 50 or 100% of the upper circular jet and central cyclone. The same broadband upper-layer disturbance (modes 1\u201332, seed 42) evolves for 500,000 seconds in every case; convection is off. Matching applies to the circular base, not its disturbance. The unmatched 2,000-km case has an initial thickness-anomaly bound of about 0.315, requiring caution about the QG approximation. Completion does not establish a stable hexagon, convergence or agreement with observed drift.",
